            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "18495664"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Involved in the breakdown of putrescine. Catalyzes the ATP-dependent gamma-glutamylation of putrescine, producing gamma-L-glutamylputrescine. Absolutely essential to utilize putrescine as both nitrogen and carbon sources and to decrease the toxicity of putrescine, which can lead to inhibition of cell growth and protein synthesis. In vitro is also able to use several diamines, and spermidine and spermine, instead of putrescine, but with a much lower activity, and cannot catalyze the gamma-glutamylation of ornithine or GABA (PubMed:18495664)"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "FUNCTION"
    },
    {
      "commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY",
      "reaction": {
        "name": "putrescine + L-glutamate + ATP = gamma-L-glutamylputrescine + ADP + phosphate + H(+)",
